# Example 15: 3D morphogenesis - L-system generates 3D plants
# Generates pseudo-3D branching structures with an extended turtle symbol set
#
# Turtle symbols (3D):
#   F    move forward one step, drawing a line
#   + -  yaw around the up axis
#   & ^  pitch around the left axis
#   / \  roll around the forward axis
#   [ ]  push / pop stack (save/restore pose)
#
# HelixLang's #lsystem renders with a 2D turtle; real 3D output is via the Python API:

#promoter name=p_grow3d strength=-0.3

#gene name=grow3d promoter=p_grow3d
ATG CTC TAA
#end

#regulate p_grow3d -> grow3d strength=+0.6

# 3D branching L-system: each iteration replaces F with a composite segment of 4 directional sub-branches
#lsystem name=plant3d axiom=F rules=0:F->FF[+F&F][-F^F][&F+F][^F-F] angle=22.5 step=1.0

